  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 138 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nThe aforementioned upper level ridge will slowly begin to drift west \nfor the middle to latter part of the work week. This will result in \nslightly cooler temperatures, with highs near seasonal normals. \nExpect highs in the mid 90s to near 100, with the hottest \ntemperatures across the Big Country. \n\nAs we head into the weekend, the upper level ridge will drift east \ntoward the Rockies. Meanwhile the ECMWF indicates a weakness in the \nridge across southwest Texas, including West Central Texas. This \nwill keep high temperatures mainly in the mid to upper 90s this \nweekend. Although an isolated shower or thunderstorm is possible, \nrain chances look too low at this time to include in the current \nforecast.",
